        openings: ("{D} and the same friend ate at a pizza place and left through a side door without paying, and the owner recognized their faces from a sheriff's flyer posted at three restaurants. The restaurant's camera shows two people walk out without stopping at the register.", "The defense will say {D} stepped outside to take a phone call and expected {D.his} friend to pay, and that the friend returned the next day and paid. {D} never meant to dine and dash."), closings: ("A flyer with two faces, a side door that avoids the register, and an unpaid check at table six, after the earlier case over {PRIOR}. {D} never came back.", "A phone call, a friend who said he would pay, and a check that was settled the next day. The State must prove {D} left meaning not to pay."),
